the late 90's, mid-90's

00:09:52.849 --> 00:09:53.940
when people where scared--

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:56.007
I was scared to go to the world wide web.

00:09:56.007 --> 00:09:57.586
There was a button up
there and it was like,

00:09:57.586 --> 00:09:58.793
the world wide web, forget it.

00:09:58.793 --> 00:10:00.093
I was in an AOL world,

00:10:00.093 --> 00:10:01.254
I'm like, that's spooky.

00:10:01.254 --> 00:10:03.042
I'm staying in here, it's safe.

00:10:03.042 --> 00:10:04.969
Facebook doesn't have that advantage,

00:10:04.969 --> 00:10:07.454
people are more educated,
they know the web exists.

00:10:07.454 --> 00:10:08.731
But in a mobile first world,

00:10:08.731 --> 00:10:12.446
in a Instagram, Facebook, WhatsApp world

00:10:12.446 --> 00:10:14.071
that's why they offered
3 billion for Snapchat.

00:10:14.071 --> 00:10:15.859
If Facebook owned Snapchat right now,

00:10:15.859 --> 00:10:17.183
they would own the entire--

00:10:17.183 --> 00:10:19.551
Alex even got excited
and he keeps it chill.

00:10:19.551 --> 00:10:20.758
I mean he said, "Pshhh." (laughs)

00:10:20.758 --> 00:10:21.734
I don't know if you heard it.

00:10:21.734 --> 00:10:23.196
They would own the ecosystem.

00:10:23.196 --> 00:10:24.404
So they're 3/4 of the way.

00:10:24.404 --> 00:10:25.727
There is some other players but,

00:10:25.727 --> 00:10:28.839
YouTube, there's other players but...

00:10:28.839 --> 00:10:31.044
I think Facebook's plan is obvious.

00:10:31.044 --> 00:10:33.506
And I think in general,
it's very interesting

00:10:33.506 --> 00:10:34.643
to watch them navigate.

00:10:34.643 --> 00:10:35.851
I think it's proper

00:10:35.851 --> 00:10:37.592
for maximizing business.

00:10:37.592 --> 00:10:39.055
It's why I'm very bullish on the company.

00:10:39.055 --> 00:10:41.446
It's why I haven't sold a
single share of the stock.

00:10:41.446 --> 00:10:43.025
I bought it private before it went public,

00:10:43.025 --> 00:10:44.488
not a share.

00:10:44.488 --> 00:10:47.124
I'm a big believer in it.

00:10:47.124 --> 00:10:48.146
Video time.

00:10:48.146 --> 00:10:49.097
- TCustomz

00:10:49.097 --> 00:10:50.320
- TCustomz, producer.

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:51.726
- Hey Gary Vee, Travis here.
- [Gary] Travis.

00:10:51.726 --> 00:10:53.289
- I first I wanna say
thanks for all you do

00:10:53.289 --> 00:10:54.096
with the #AskGaryVee Show.

00:10:54.096 --> 00:10:56.198
Most definitely will be buying 
the book when it releases.

00:10:56.198 --> 00:10:58.569
Question for you, is you
talk a lot about the use

00:10:58.569 --> 00:11:00.218
of Twitter Native Video
and I can personally say

00:11:00.218 --> 00:11:03.074
I've seen a lot of really
great results with engagement.

00:11:03.074 --> 00:11:04.513
It almost got my reamped

00:11:04.513 --> 00:11:06.208
about using the Twitter platform again.

00:11:06.208 --> 00:11:08.298
You foresee this type of
video response funtionality

00:11:08.298 --> 00:11:10.667
being built in natively
in some of the more common

00:11:10.667 --> 00:11:12.547
email clients anytime in the near future?

00:11:12.547 --> 00:11:14.242
Would this be practical
for someone like you

00:11:14.242 --> 00:11:16.982
who travels a lot and who has
a lot of mass email volume

00:11:16.982 --> 00:11:18.004
to go through?

00:11:18.004 --> 00:11:19.920
Would love to hear your
thoughts, thanks for your time.

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:21.834
- Travis, way to keep it tight.

00:11:21.834 --> 00:11:23.461
He like went Bone Thugs on that.

00:11:23.461 --> 00:11:24.082
(laughs)

00:11:24.082 --> 00:11:25.407
Real fast.

00:11:25.407 --> 00:11:27.269
I watched Straight Out
Of Compton last night.

00:11:27.269 --> 00:11:28.383
- [Staphon] That was good.

00:11:28.383 --> 00:11:29.846
- Oh my god, I loved it.

00:11:29.846 --> 00:11:31.290
Loved it.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.166
(sighs)

00:11:35.616 --> 00:11:38.035
What I think is really interesting on that

00:11:38.035 --> 00:11:41.797
is I made, (laughs) I wish Erik
Kastner was here right now.

00:11:41.797 --> 00:11:45.182
Let's show Kastner's
Twitter profile @kastner.

00:11:45.182 --> 00:11:46.859
K-A-S-T-N-E-R

00:11:46.859 --> 00:11:49.088
Erik was the developer
that sat right next to me

00:11:49.088 --> 00:11:51.456
that helped me build up WineLibrary.com

00:11:51.456 --> 00:11:55.268
And I made a prediction to him in 2004

00:11:55.268 --> 00:11:57.482
or five or six or seven

00:11:57.482 --> 00:12:00.072
that all email would be video

00:12:00.072 --> 00:12:01.834
in five to seven years.

00:12:01.834 --> 00:12:04.365
I'm glad we weren't doing the
Ask #GaryVeeShow back then

00:12:04.365 --> 00:12:05.642
'cause boy that highlight--

00:12:05.642 --> 00:12:07.430
The lowlights of this show, by the way,

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:09.334
I can't wait for the
lowlights in a couple years

00:12:09.334 --> 00:12:10.983
of all my wrong things in this

00:12:10.983 --> 00:12:12.817
'cause those are fun too.

00:12:14.287 --> 00:12:16.361
(laughs) Not really.

00:12:16.361 --> 00:12:18.196
I think the answer's no.

00:12:18.196 --> 00:12:20.100
I think that what people don't realize

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:23.559
is most people don't want to be on camera.

00:12:23.559 --> 00:12:24.929
And this is a really interesting thing.

00:12:24.929 --> 00:12:26.833
Now, what's happening right now

00:12:26.833 --> 00:12:29.387
with everybody growing
up in selfie culture

00:12:29.387 --> 00:12:32.824
and all these 15, 14, 13 year
olds just owning this move.

00:12:32.824 --> 00:12:34.844
I do think that behavior's changing.

00:12:34.844 --> 00:12:37.700
And I do think that video's upside

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:40.649
over a 15 to 30 year period,

00:12:40.649 --> 00:12:42.018
15 to 30 years from now,

00:12:42.018 --> 00:12:44.433
15 through 30 years from now

00:12:44.433 --> 00:12:47.614
is very high because I think
we're training youngsters,

00:12:47.614 --> 00:12:50.192
7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, to be more out.

00:12:50.192 --> 00:12:51.213
(phone dings)

00:12:51.213 --> 00:12:52.583
To be more in front of the camera,

00:12:52.583 --> 00:12:54.162
it's not this kind of thing anymore.

00:12:54.162 --> 00:12:58.481
I'm bullish on the concept.

00:12:58.481 --> 00:13:02.707
I do think email is ripe for a change

00:13:02.707 --> 00:13:04.634
in the next generation.

00:13:04.634 --> 00:13:06.352
I think, you know, Gmail's

00:13:06.352 --> 00:13:08.233
gotten heavy, it started off lighter.

00:13:08.233 --> 00:13:09.579
I think there's some real opportunity.

00:13:09.579 --> 00:13:11.855
I do think when you look at Slack

00:13:11.855 --> 00:13:14.154
and how people use that in
companies to communicate,

00:13:14.154 --> 00:13:17.706
I think a version of texting,
Twitter video and email,

00:13:17.706 --> 00:13:20.585
the Frankenstein of that,
eight, nine years from now

00:13:20.585 --> 00:13:21.491
has a real shot.

00:13:21.491 --> 00:13:22.536
And then there's gonna be a technology

00:13:22.536 --> 00:13:23.766
we don't understand, like holograms.

00:13:23.766 --> 00:13:25.368
Like Princess Leia pops up

00:13:25.368 --> 00:13:26.227
in Star Wars.

00:13:26.227 --> 00:13:27.806
I'd like that even better, I'd be like,

00:13:27.806 --> 00:13:28.851
yo, I could use my hands.

00:13:28.851 --> 00:13:29.803
It'd be great.

00:13:29.803 --> 00:13:32.613
So I think a lot of technology will come

00:13:32.613 --> 00:13:34.911
and I do think there'll be change.

00:13:34.911 --> 00:13:37.349
I do think that video and email clients

00:13:37.349 --> 00:13:39.276
like Gmail and Apple mail

00:13:39.276 --> 00:13:41.297
is gonna be smaller than you think

00:13:41.297 --> 00:13:43.317
because people don't
like to go that route.

00:13:43.317 --> 00:13:45.104
It actually takes longer

00:13:45.104 --> 00:13:46.707
and I think time is the biggest asset.

00:13:46.707 --> 00:13:49.400
I think people can type it
quicker than click, dah-dah-dah

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:52.720
And I think we're writing less.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:54.206
You know, a lot more emoji's.

00:13:54.206 --> 00:13:58.246
These guys will probably
laugh right now. (laughs)

00:13:58.246 --> 00:14:00.220
My emails are tight.

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:01.544
(laughs)

00:14:01.544 --> 00:14:04.841
They're very much in the
K, LOL, Cool, Go, Yes, No

00:14:04.841 --> 00:14:07.557
I mean, I am keeping it tight.

00:14:07.557 --> 00:14:10.251
When I write two to three
sentences, people are like,

00:14:10.251 --> 00:14:11.737
Whoa.

00:14:11.737 --> 00:14:15.405
I think time is the biggest variable

00:14:15.405 --> 00:14:19.144
besides people's non want
to be in picture form.

00:14:19.144 --> 00:14:20.328
Think of how many people don't wanna

00:14:20.328 --> 00:14:21.651
take pictures of themselves.

00:14:21.651 --> 00:14:22.696
They don't wanna see themselves.

00:14:22.696 --> 00:14:24.716
That's a very big culture, underrated.

00:14:24.716 --> 00:14:26.968
Especially for the generation
that's in the workforce now.

00:14:26.968 --> 00:14:30.312
The younger generation I think
will change that over time.

00:14:30.312 --> 00:14:32.007
- Oh, Rue, Ree, Rue.

00:14:32.007 --> 00:14:33.905
I mean, I know him really well, I just--

00:14:33.905 --> 00:14:34.514
- I know.

00:14:34.514 --> 00:14:35.443
- I interact with him a lot.

00:14:35.443 --> 00:14:36.550
I just don't know if he pronounces it Roo.

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:38.360
- [Voiceover] Rui asks,

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:39.866
"You don't talk much about Tumblr.

00:14:39.866 --> 00:14:41.926
"Do you think it's losing relevance?"

00:14:41.926 --> 00:14:43.499
- Yes.

00:14:45.083 --> 00:14:46.175
You keep asking quest--

00:14:46.175 --> 00:14:47.661
(laughs)

00:14:47.661 --> 00:14:48.938
Yes, I do think it's losing relevance.

00:14:48.938 --> 00:14:50.401
I think Tumblr lost its moment,

00:14:50.401 --> 00:14:51.678
which is tough for me 'cause I was

00:14:51.678 --> 00:14:52.769
an early investor in Tumblr.

00:14:52.769 --> 00:14:54.510
I made a lot of money
when it sold to Yahoo!

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:55.764
but it's part of a bigger company

00:14:55.764 --> 00:14:58.179
that's selling media in a traditional way

00:14:58.179 --> 00:14:59.549
even though it's Yahoo!

00:14:59.549 --> 00:15:02.080
And I think that it lost to Instagram

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.960
in the mobile translation

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:06.004
much like many people did.

00:15:06.004 --> 00:15:08.952
It is still a very high
rated app in the app store,

00:15:08.952 --> 00:15:10.694
if you look in the top 100, it's usually

00:15:10.694 --> 00:15:12.784
around number 90 to 110.

00:15:12.784 --> 00:15:15.965
But I do think it's losing relevance.

00:15:15.965 --> 00:15:17.451
I think there's a lot
of people that love it,

00:15:17.451 --> 00:15:18.728
it's still a very big platform

00:15:18.728 --> 00:15:21.328
but I don't say huge growth in it.

00:15:21.328 --> 00:15:22.814
I don't see it.

00:15:22.814 --> 00:15:25.020
I think it's a niche now,

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:27.272
where a lot of creative
people are doing their thing,

00:15:27.272 --> 00:15:28.503
it's a great creative outlet.

00:15:28.503 --> 00:15:30.964
A lot of people are doing
their anonymous work on it.

00:15:30.964 --> 00:15:32.682
But then Snapchat came along

00:15:32.682 --> 00:15:34.052
and kinda created a world--

00:15:34.052 --> 00:15:35.445
India, what's going on behind me?

00:15:35.445 --> 00:15:36.653
- [India] Nothing, I was just waving to--

00:15:36.653 --> 00:15:37.883
(slaps table)

00:15:41.843 --> 00:15:43.840
- What, no, no, you were laughing before.

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:44.908
- [India] No, I wasn't.

00:15:44.908 --> 00:15:46.092
- Okay, I'll have to watch
that part of the show.

00:15:46.092 --> 00:15:47.532
(laughs)

00:15:47.532 --> 00:15:49.319
I think, the show.

00:15:49.319 --> 00:15:52.524
I do think Tumblr's lost its momentum

00:15:52.524 --> 00:15:55.844
and would need to have
some real innovation

00:15:55.844 --> 00:15:58.537
to get going again.

00:15:58.537 --> 00:16:00.023
Yes, I don't talk about it a lot

00:16:00.023 --> 00:16:03.245
because it's not atop of mind.

00:16:03.245 --> 00:16:05.322
And it's a current show, right.

00:16:05.322 --> 00:16:07.574
Like this is gonna always follow

00:16:07.574 --> 00:16:09.850
the path of what I think is most going on.

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:12.195
Just wanna thank everybody
for watching the show.

00:16:12.195 --> 00:16:14.842
I realized over this weekend,
little bit over the break

00:16:14.842 --> 00:16:17.210
of just how much this
community means to me.

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:19.532
Really enjoyed the amount of people

00:16:19.532 --> 00:16:21.552
that have jumped out of lurkerville

00:16:21.552 --> 00:16:23.293
and started commenting,

00:16:23.293 --> 00:16:24.361
it really means a lot to me.

00:16:24.361 --> 00:16:26.498
It is absolutely my oxygen,

00:16:26.498 --> 00:16:29.005
in lieu of the financial aspects.

00:16:29.005 --> 00:16:31.583
As many books as I sell of Ask Gary Vee,

00:16:31.583 --> 00:16:33.951
the time commitment doesn't work mathwise

00:16:33.951 --> 00:16:36.366
so I ask myself, what is it really?

00:16:36.366 --> 00:16:38.386
And I think it's our interaction.

00:16:38.386 --> 00:16:40.499
And I definitely think
it's our interaction.

00:16:40.499 --> 00:16:42.658
Thank you so much for a lot
of people that jumped out

00:16:42.658 --> 00:16:44.516
over the weekend and said, "I'm a lurker,

00:16:44.516 --> 00:16:46.698
here's my comment on the latest show."

00:16:46.698 --> 00:16:49.879
Question of the day.

00:16:49.879 --> 00:16:52.097
What do I wanna know about?

00:16:52.097 --> 00:16:53.773
Labor Day's coming up.

00:16:53.773 --> 00:16:55.398
It's so funny these questions
of the day are becoming harder

00:16:55.398 --> 00:16:58.161
because I really don't
know what I want to know.

00:16:58.161 --> 00:16:59.763
They've become less self- serving

00:16:59.763 --> 00:17:01.783
from a datas perspective.

00:17:01.783 --> 00:17:03.989
Question of the day.

00:17:03.989 --> 00:17:05.429
When is your fav--

00:17:05.429 --> 00:17:06.938
I guess, I'm going self-serving.

00:17:06.938 --> 00:17:08.819
What is your favorite football team?

00:17:08.819 --> 00:17:10.954
And what, after one preseason game,

00:17:10.954 --> 00:17:14.740
is the prediction for your
team's record this year?

00:17:14.740 --> 00:17:18.686
Side note, I may change
question of the day.

00:17:18.686 --> 00:17:19.941
As a matter of fact, I'm changing it.

00:17:19.941 --> 00:17:22.518
Right here on the spot,
we're going improv.

00:17:22.518 --> 00:17:24.165
No more question of the day, this is it.

00:17:24.165 --> 00:17:25.420
This will be part of the--

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:26.395
This is 132?

00:17:26.395 --> 00:17:27.835
This will be part of
the quiz game one day.

00:17:27.835 --> 00:17:29.530
What episode did it go
from question of the day

00:17:29.530 --> 00:17:31.550
to comment of the day.

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:34.104
Please make your comment on the content

00:17:34.104 --> 00:17:35.776
that you just watched.

00:17:35.776 --> 00:17:37.332
You keep asking questions,

00:17:37.332 --> 00:17:39.584
I'll keep answering them.

00:17:39.584 --> 00:17:42.109
(hip hop music)

